# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same two variables in your host.
#
# Both values below are for the DEVELOPMENT project (treatment-ops-dev), which holds fictional data
# only. They are safe to commit and safe to ship in a browser bundle:
#
#   - VITE_SUPABASE_URL is a public endpoint.
#   - The publishable key carries no privileges of its own. It identifies the project; every request
#     it makes is still evaluated by RLS against the signed-in user. An anonymous request with this
#     key reads nothing, because no table grants access without an assignment.
#
# What must NEVER appear in this file, in any VITE_ variable, or anywhere in this repository:
#
#   - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. It bypasses RLS entirely. Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into
#     the browser bundle and is therefore public. Server environments only.
#   - Production project credentials. Production gets its own values, set in the host's secret store.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ygustqrxjaqfbdjftcmq.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_9Owtf9HkLDe8pi5mkFDukQ_KJ3Flq0X
